# Character facing (Groyper & Meshy rigs)

Imported Meshy FBX characters (Groyper, Sheriff, etc.) bind facing **-Z**, not +Z. The visual `Model` node needs a **PI (180°) yaw offset** so locomotion and look-at match world movement.

## groyper_body.tscn scene correction

`groyper_body.tscn` already applies a **180° Y flip on the `Body` node** (`Transform3D(-1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, -1)`). Do **not** add a `Skeleton3D` transform on top — that double-flips the mesh and turns the overworld player backward. Saddle/riding poses belong in `saddle.tres`, not baked into the skeleton rest pose in the scene file.

## Groyper characters (NPCs, duelists, AI)

Use `GroyperBodyUtils` when the **CharacterBody3D root does not rotate** and only `Model` turns:

```gdscript
_model.rotation.y = GroyperBodyUtils.MODEL_YAW_OFFSET
var target_yaw := GroyperBodyUtils.facing_yaw_for_direction(direction)
_model.rotation.y = lerp_angle(_model.rotation.y, target_yaw, FACING_SPEED * delta)
```

## Groyper overworld player (exception)

`groyper_overworld_player.gd` uses a **camera pivot** (`CameraPivot.rotation.y = _camera_yaw`). Do **not** use `facing_yaw_for_direction()` for movement facing — it double-applies PI and turns the player backward.

```gdscript
# _ready: idle mesh alignment with camera
_model.rotation.y = GroyperBodyUtils.MODEL_YAW_OFFSET

# _update_facing: raw atan2 only
var target_yaw := atan2(move_dir.x, move_dir.z)
```

`move_dir` is already camera-relative; the pivot owns the yaw offset.

## Sheriff / other Meshy town NPCs

Use `MeshyLocomotionUtils.MODEL_YAW_OFFSET` and `MeshyLocomotionUtils.facing_yaw_for_direction()` — same PI rule.

## Horses and custom rigs

Horse `Facing.rotation.y` uses plain `atan2(dir.x, dir.z)` — same as the overworld player. Do not add PI on top.
Optional `mesh_yaw_offset` export on `StupidHorse` fixes the imported mesh only.

## Common mistake

```gdscript
# BAD for town NPCs — faces backward when walking
var yaw := atan2(dir.x, dir.z)

# GOOD for town NPCs / AI (no camera pivot)
var yaw := GroyperBodyUtils.facing_yaw_for_direction(dir)

# BAD for overworld player — double PI with camera pivot
var yaw := GroyperBodyUtils.facing_yaw_for_direction(move_dir)

# GOOD for overworld player
var yaw := atan2(move_dir.x, move_dir.z)
```

## Spawn markers

`Marker3D` rotation sets the **CharacterBody3D** root. The **Model** child still needs `MODEL_YAW_OFFSET` in code after the rig is spawned.

### Groyper overworld player spawns

The overworld player is the exception to “only Model turns”:

1. Apply **`spawn.global_rotation`** to the **CharacterBody3D** root (same as other spawn markers).
2. After placement, call **`sync_overworld_spawn_orientation()`** so `CameraPivot` stays at the default explore yaw (`PI`) and `Model.rotation.y` is `MODEL_YAW_OFFSET`.
3. Do **not** copy marker yaw onto `CameraPivot` alone while zeroing the root — that breaks the root × pivot facing pair and flips the camera or mesh.

Movement facing still uses raw `atan2(move_dir.x, move_dir.z)` on the Model; never `facing_yaw_for_direction()` on the overworld player.
